      "ciStep": "proof-capture-authorization-guard",
      "notes": "Proof/evidence capture is authorized by the SAME execution right that authorizes the work it proves. Structurally joins the role->permission maps (permissions.go rolePermissions + permissions_orgrole.go tierPermissions) to the route table (routes.go protectedRoutes) and re-implements AuthorizeRoute's AND/OR semantics: every role holding any *Execute permission MUST be authorized for every /app/proofs write route. Catches the 2026-08-03 shipped defect where the proof routes were gated on the vaccination-era TaskExecute alone, so a growth_director (WeighingExecute, deliberately NOT TaskExecute) could record a weighing observation but 403'd on POST /app/proofs/uploads -- no proof ever reached SYNCED and lump-sum Submit stayed permanently disabled. Self-test includes an adversarial reconstruction of that exact defect plus a future-vertical case (a new *Execute permission with no proof access), so a new vertical cannot repeat it. Blind spots are enumerated in the script header: runtime-composed grants, handler-level authorization inside a proof endpoint, scope/tenant narrowing, evidence surfaces outside /app/proofs, and AdminOnly routes."
    },
